  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Boeing has $9.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Boeing won 569 awards so far this fiscal year and the average award size is $16M. Obligations are up 108.2% year over year. Boeing obligations by fiscal year show swings: $7.3B in FY21, $3.9B in FY22, $3.3B in FY23, $5B in FY24, $4.4B in FY25 and $9.1B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $9.1B in FY2026 to date; the General Services Administration shows $0. Boeing sells across several NAICS markets. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market at $9B. Other listed markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $72M, Computer Systems Design Services at $14.4M, Engineering Services at $7M, Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $506K, Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals at $356K, and Hardware Manufacturing at $7.9K. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date), and award-value figures in some tables are total contract values while the rest are obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Boeing's federal sales?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounts for Boeing federal obligations in FY2026 to date, with $9.1B. Aircraft Manufacturing dominates Boeing's federal markets at $9B. Other markets are much smaller, for example Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $72M and Computer Systems Design Services at $14.4M. Several listed markets show minimal or zero obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have Boeing's federal obligations changed over time?",
        "body": "Boeing obligations varied across fiscal years: $7.3B in FY21, $3.9B in FY22, $3.3B in FY23, $5B in FY24, $4.4B in FY25 and $9.1B in FY26. Obligations rose year over year into FY2026, with an increase described as up 108.2%. The current FY2026 total is a fiscal year to date figure and therefore partial."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Boeing make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Boeing makes $9.1B from federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Boeing won 569 awards so far this fiscal year and the average award size is $16M. Obligations are up 108.2% year over year. The fiscal-year history shows obligations of $7.3B in FY21, $3.9B in FY22, $3.3B in FY23, $5B in FY24 and $4.4B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Boeing?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense buys from Boeing, obligating $9.1B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration shows $0 in obligations for Boeing in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Boeing sell to the government?",
      "a": "Boeing sells primarily Aircraft Manufacturing products to the government, with $9B in that market. Boeing also has obligations in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $72M, Computer Systems Design Services at $14.4M, and Engineering Services at $7M, plus smaller amounts in instrument and hardware manufacturing categories such as $506K, $356K and $7.9K."
    },
